Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{"action": "final", "output": {
  "research_concepts": [
    "player absence",
    "offensive reorganization (identity displacement D_A)",
    "structural influence load L",
    "points per possession (PPP) change",
    "reorganization relative to L"
  ],
  "methodological_questions": [
    "How to define reorganization relative to L: e.g., residual D_A after controlling for L, or D_A/L ratio?",
    "How to estimate PPP change across absence spells while controlling for opponent strength and context?",
    "What sample size of absence spells is available, and is it sufficient for correlation/regression?",
    "How to avoid mechanical link between play-type mix change (D_A) and PPP change?",
    "How to handle potential confounding from lineup changes, opponent quality, and missing players?"
  ],
  "historical_evidence": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-014",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Real on/off absence of a shaper displaces the team fingerprint more than a usage-matched non-shaper, and LOO L(p) tracks observed D_A. Delta D_A=+0.115, t=6.35, p~7e-9, shaper larger in 81% of pairs; r(L,D_A)=+0.60 (shapers +0.79)."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence. Unmatched conn vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08; paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050",
      "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
      "finding": "Identified opponent play-type suppressors (e.g., PUTBACK) that lower star next-possession PPP, with effect sizes like D. Mitchell from 1.178 to 0.884."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022",
      "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
      "finding": "Rank-1 suppressor varies across players, but deltas mostly within 1-2 SE with no multiple-comparison control; OTHER artifact flagged."
    }
  ],
  "failed_approaches": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022",
      "what_failed": "Identifying star-specific suppression triggers without multiplicity control",
      "why": "Deltas mostly within 1-2 SE and no correction for multiple comparison; OTHER artifact flagged, leading to inconclusive verdict."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050",
      "what_failed": "Not a hypothesis test",
      "why": "Descriptive study of opponent play suppression; no planned hypothesis, no multiplicity correction, and small n_after cells (32-95)."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_establishes": [
    "Offensive identity displacement D_A is a measurable, reliable index of reorganization during a player absence.",
    "Structural influence L is positively correlated with D_A (r=0.60 overall, stronger for shapers).",
    "D_A varies systematically by player type (connectors/shapers show larger displacement than usage-matched role players)."
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish": [
    "Whether reorganization (D_A) or its deviation from L predicts the change in points per possession.",
    "The direction, magnitude, or sign of any relationship between D_A and PPP change.",
    "Whether such a relationship would hold after controlling for opponent quality, lineup context, and pre-absence PPP.",
    "The power needed to detect a plausible effect size in the available sample of absence spells."
  ],
  "own_inferences": [
    "The research question can be operationalized as a linear regression: ΔPPP_i ~ D_A_i + L_i + controls, where ΔPPP is change in points per 100 possessions and D_A is identity displacement during the absence.",
    "Using L as a covariate in the model isolates the portion of reorganization that is not simply due to the player's structural influence, capturing the idea 'relative to L'.",
    "The 148 absence spells are likely the maximum sample; after excluding spells with too few pre/during games and outliers, the effective sample will be smaller, raising power concerns.",
    "Even if an association is detected, it may not generalize beyond the seasons included because team composition, style, and rules evolve.",
    "The mechanic of D_A being derived from play-type mix and PPP being an aggregate over the same possessions creates a potential for composition-driven correlation that must be interpreted carefully.",
    "Pre-registration is essential: specify the exact regression model, control variables, handling of missing data, and the primary test statistic before analyzing the targeted seasons (2024-26)."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "True effect size unknown; pilot estimates from 2022-23 season could provide a prior, but no such analysis has been reported.",
    "The noise in D_A estimates for spells with few games may dominate the signal; trade-off between spell length and sample size.",
    "Structural influence L is computed from pre-absence games and is thus a different temporal window; its ability to serve as a control for expected D_A may be affected by player role changes or team scheme shifts.",
    "The concept 'reorganization relative to L' could also be interpreted as D_A/L ratio; the choice between regression with L covariate and ratio analysis could change the results.",
    "Potential carry-over effects if multiple absences per team per season are included; spells may not be independent."
  ],
  "historical_effect": {
    "changed_decision": "no",
    "explanation": "No prior study tested the exact hypothesis. The retrieved evidence provides a foundation (measurement of D_A and L, and their correlation) but does not directly answer or pre-empt the proposed test. Therefore the decision to proceed with a pre-registered design is unchanged by the historical record."
  },
  "testability": {
    "p_testable": 0.7,
    "blocking_constraints": [
      {
        "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
        "text": "Only 148 spells are available; after filtering for minimum games (e.g., 5 pre, 5 during) the sample will be smaller, possibly below 120. Detecting a medium correlation (r~0.2) would require ~150 for 80% power, making marginal."
      },
      {
        "code": "CONFOUNDING",
        "text": "Opponent defensive strength and game location influence both play-type mix (and thus D_A) and points per possession. Without adequate control, associations may be spurious."
      }
    ]
  },
  "prior_work": {
    "already_answered": "partly",
    "cited": [
      "FAM:SF-PAP-014",
      "FAM:SF-APPS-088"
    ],
    "summary": "Prior work established that offensive identity displacement D_A is a valid reorganization measure, that structural influence L predicts D_A (r=0.60), and that player type affects the magnitude of displacement. However, it did not examine whether deviation from L predicts changes in points per possession during absence spells."
  },
  "risks": [
    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "Limited number of absence spells (max 148) reduces power to detect realistic effect sizes; regression with multiple covariates further decreases effective degrees of freedom."
    },
    {
      "code": "CONFOUNDING",
      "text": "Opponent quality, home/road, other simultaneous player absences, and game script can confound the relationship between D_A and ΔPPP. Unless controlled, effect estimates may be biased."
    },
    {
      "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
      "text": "D_A is computed from a limited number of games per spell; noise may attenuate correlations. L also may be noisy for players with few pre-absence games."
    },
    {
      "code": "MECHANICAL_FLOOR",
      "text": "If using D_A/L as predictor, players with very low L will produce extreme and unstable ratios. Regression with L as covariate avoids this but introduces moderate collinearity."
    },
    {
      "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
      "text": "The predictor D_A is computed from the same games that contribute to ΔPPP; while this is a cross-sectional association, it limits causal interpretation and can create composition-driven correlations."
    },
    {
      "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
      "text": "Exploratory examination of multiple definitions (ratio, residual, different minimum-game thresholds) could inflate Type I error if not pre-registered."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome": {
    "supported": 0.3,
    "rejected": 0.2,
    "untestable": 0.1,
    "artifact": 0.1,
    "uncertain": 0.3
  },
  "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "Partial linear effect of offensive identity displacement D_A on the change in points per 100 possessions (ΔPPP) during a player's absence spell, holding constant structural influence L and other control variables.",
    "unit": "One player absence spell (continuous absence of a single player from a team, with minimum pre and during games).",
    "sample": "All player absence spells from NBA 2022-23 through 2025-26 seasons (regular season and playoffs) that have at least 5 games of pre-absence data and at least 5 games during the absence, excluding garbage time. To avoid double-counting overlapping absences, for each team-season a spell is excluded if it overlaps another spell by more than 20% of its games. Total expected spells ~100-120.",
    "power": "Based on an expected partial correlation of 0.2 (small-medium effect), a sample of 100 spells yields ~50% power at alpha 0.05 two-sided; 140 yields ~65%. The analysis will be reported with confidence intervals and will be considered exploratory if the final sample falls below 100.",
    "controls": [
      "Average opponent defensive rating (points per 100 possessions allowed) across the games of the absence spell, weighted by possessions.",
      "Proportion of home games during the absence spell.",
      "Pre-absence team offensive rating (points per 100 possessions).",
      "Length of absence spell (number of games).",
      "Player's pre-absence structural influence L.",
      "Indicator for whether the spell involved a coordinator/shaper (optional sensitivity check)."
    ],
    "falsification": [
      "Placebo test: randomly assign absence spells to different players from the same team and recalculate D_A; the association should disappear.",
      "Sensitivity test: compute D_A using only the first 3 games of the absence spell (to reduce overlap with full-spell PPP) and check if direction holds.",
      "Control for same-season lineup-weighted opponent defensive rating to ensure no residual confounding."
    ],
    "multiplicity": "A single pre-registered primary model (ΔPPP ~ D_A + L + opponent_def_rtg + home_prop + pre_PPP) will be tested; any alternative definitions will be reported as exploratory. No adjustment for multiple endpoints.",
    "decision_rule": "Reject the null hypothesis of no association if the two-sided p-value for the coefficient of D_A is < 0.05. A positive coefficient indicates that greater reorganization (beyond L) is associated with an increase in PPP; a negative coefficient a decrease. The primary analysis will use robust standard errors."
  }
}}

